{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Here is a GCSE-style question. Fibreglass and wool felt are used for loft insulation. A thicker layer of wool felt is needed to give the same insulation as fibreglass. Part A, worth two marks: which material has the higher thermal conductivity, and why? Wool felt has the higher conductivity, so a greater thickness is needed to achieve a similar resistance to conduction. Award one mark for wool felt and one for the explanation. Part B, worth two marks: explain why trapped air helps reduce energy transfer. Air has low thermal conductivity, so conduction through it is slow; trapping the air in small pockets also prevents large convection currents. Award one mark for each correct explanation.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 48.666122, "words": [["Here", 0.0], ["is", 0.372], ["a", 0.627], ["GCSE-style", 0.731], ["question.", 1.73], ["Fibreglass", 2.252], ["and", 2.914], ["wool", 3.077], ["felt", 3.437], ["are", 3.889], ["used", 4.18], ["for", 4.551], ["loft", 4.748], ["insulation.", 5.027], ["A", 5.828], ["thicker", 6.002], ["layer", 6.339], ["of", 6.618], ["wool", 6.745], ["felt", 7.047], ["is", 7.465], ["needed", 7.709], ["to", 8.069], ["give", 8.197], ["the", 8.406], ["same", 8.533], ["insulation", 8.8], ["as", 9.532], ["fibreglass.", 9.845], ["Part", 10.693], ["A,", 11.088], ["worth", 11.622], ["two", 11.935], ["marks:", 12.098], ["which", 13.166], ["material", 13.502], ["has", 14.153], ["the", 14.373], ["higher", 14.536], ["thermal", 14.895], ["conductivity,", 15.302], ["and", 16.323], ["why?", 16.637], ["Wool", 17.055], ["felt", 17.345], ["has", 17.786], ["the", 18.042], ["higher", 18.251], ["conductivity,", 18.645], ["so", 19.655], ["a", 19.957], ["greater", 20.062], ["thickness", 20.491], ["is", 21.037], ["needed", 21.211], ["to", 21.548], ["achieve", 21.699], ["a", 22.128], ["similar", 22.302], ["resistance", 22.778], ["to", 23.405], ["conduction.", 23.556], ["Award", 24.578], ["o